```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, count(*) n, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.ready' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search container readiness is 0 across all 23 abnormal samples, so the search instance never became ready."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, metric, count(*) n, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='search' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, metric, count(*), min(value), max(value) FROM normal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_deployment_name='search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search restarts rose from 0 in normal to 3–6 during the incident, showing a crash loop."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search emits no spans during the incident, versus 650 search.Search/Nearby server spans in normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, attr_span_kind, span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,3) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "673 of 678 frontend calls to search.Search/Nearby error out in about 0.03 ms, a fast connection failure."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend HTTP /hotels returns 500 with Error status for 673 abnormal requests; normal has none."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Summary:** The user-visible degradation is on `/hotels`, served by `frontend`. Almost all of those requests now fail with HTTP 500. The cause is the `search` service, which is crash-looping (restarts 0→6, never ready) and emits no spans during the incident. Frontend's `search.Search/Nearby` calls fail almost instantly. The drops in `geo`, `rate`, `profile` and `reservation` spans are downstream effects of `/hotels` no longer reaching them, not separate faults. Geo's restart count of 7 is the same in normal and abnormal periods, so it is not part of this incident. There are no `hubble_*` network metrics, so this is not a network fault.

I labelled the fault `pod_unavailable`. `pod_failure` is the equivalent label under the scoring rules; the data fits either one.
